{{- $f := includeTemplate "facts.tmpl" . | fromYaml }}
# The i-have-adhd plugin was retired to a skill-only delivery. Deleting the
# managed source stopped chezmoi managing the extracted archive, but an
# already-deployed copy survives until pruned here. Its ~/.omp/agent flag is
# pruned by the omp block below, with the rest of that tree's managed targets.
.local/share/i-have-adhd

# Orphaned compound-engineering skills. They used to be fetched into
# ~/.agents/skills/ by the dotagents `[[skills]] name = "*"` wildcard entry;
# that entry is gone, because the plugin is now installed natively per agent
# (see the compound-engineering section in AGENTS.md). dotagents does NOT prune
# skill directories it no longer declares — its lock file drops them but the
# dirs stay, and its `sync` cannot run here at all (the chezmoi-managed
# ~/.agents/agents.toml is 0400, so sync's rewrite of it EACCESes). Left behind,
# every ce-* skill would load TWICE: once as a stale directory here and once
# from the plugin.
#
# Safe: these `ce-*` / `lfg` patterns match neither the external skill deployed
# there (`improve`) nor the locally-authored chezmoi-managed
# skills under dot_agents/skills/<name>/ (`daily-report`); dotagents will never
# re-create the ce-* dirs now that the wildcard entry is gone.
.agents/skills/ce-*
.agents/skills/lfg

# The playwright-cli external skill was retired from .chezmoidata/agents.yaml;
# deleting the source declaration stops managing it but leaves the
# already-deployed ~/.agents/skills/playwright-cli directory behind — prune it
# here.
.agents/skills/playwright-cli

# Removed shared hub + its @AGENTS.md mirror. The user-scoped instruction core
# is composed by .chezmoitemplates/agents-instructions.tmpl and rendered into
# the managed omp wrapper (~/.omp/agent/AGENTS.md), so the legacy shared
# ~/.agents/AGENTS.md hub and its ~/.agents/CLAUDE.md mirror no longer have a
# source. Deleting the dot_agents source files stopped managing them but did
# not delete the already-deployed copies — prune them here.
.agents/AGENTS.md
.agents/CLAUDE.md

# Stray empty Codex target. dot_codex/readonly_codex.toml was a 0-byte file
# that Codex never reads: its configuration lives in ~/.codex/config.toml, which
# the codex settings reconciler asserts leaf by leaf. Deleting the source
# stopped managing it but did not delete the already-deployed 0444 copy — prune
# it here. There is NO gate: dot_codex/ was never ignored on any OS or in
# containers, so every host received the file, and it holds no live state.
.codex/codex.toml

# The omp harness was retired: dot_omp/ and the four phase-70 reconcilers are
# gone, so nothing deploys into ~/.omp/agent any more. Every path below was
# WRITTEN BY CHEZMOI and is un-written here, one entry per managed target rather
# than a directory entry, because ~/.omp/ also holds state omp itself created —
# agent.db carries live Figma OAuth tokens — and apply must not reach it. The
# operator removes the binary and the remaining runtime state by hand; see
# docs/decommission/omp.md.
#
# .env is included: run_after_config-omp-auth.sh.tmpl resolved EXA_API_KEY from
# 1Password and wrote it there in plaintext, so leaving it behind strands a live
# credential in a directory nothing manages any more.
.omp/agent/AGENTS.md
.omp/agent/CLAUDE.md
.omp/agent/mcp.json
.omp/agent/models.yml
.omp/agent/APPEND_SYSTEM.md
.omp/agent/TITLE_SYSTEM.md
.omp/agent/.i-have-adhd-always
.omp/agent/.env
.omp/agent/agents/claude.md
.omp/agent/agents/gemini.md
.omp/agent/rules/comment-c-family.md
.omp/agent/rules/comment-dash.md
.omp/agent/rules/comment-hash.md
.omp/agent/rules/comment-html.md
.omp/agent/rules/comment-ocaml.md
.omp/agent/rules/comment-python-docstring.md

# The garden project registry moved from ~/src/garden.yaml to
# ~/.config/garden/garden.yaml so ~/src holds only project trees. Deleting the
# old source stops managing the old target but leaves the already-deployed 0444
# copy behind — prune it here, in the target-application phase, so no stale
# registry is visible to the 90-src reconcile script that runs last.
#
# GATED to the platforms that actually received the old target. The encrypted
# registry was chezmoiignored in containers (no GPG key: 80-keys is bash-only),
# so chezmoi never deployed ~/src/garden.yaml there. An ungated prune would
# delete a same-named file those hosts own, which chezmoi did not put there — a
# destructive removal of user data, not a cleanup.
{{- if not $f.container }}
src/garden.yaml
{{- end }}

# The GPG secrets cache was removed, so
# dot_local/bin/executable_chezmoi-secrets-sync.tmpl no longer has a source.
# Deleting that source stopped chezmoi managing it but left the
# already-deployed ~/.local/bin/chezmoi-secrets-sync executable behind — prune
# it here. There is NO container gate: the container ignore rules do not exclude
# .local/bin, so containers received this binary too and must prune it.
.local/bin/chezmoi-secrets-sync

# The Z.ai coding plan expired, so dot_local/bin/executable_claude-glm.tmpl —
# whose only backend was https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic — no longer has a
# source. Deleting that source stopped chezmoi managing it but left the
# already-deployed ~/.local/bin/claude-glm executable behind, still on PATH and
# still pointed at a dead endpoint — prune it here. There is NO container gate,
# for the same reason as chezmoi-secrets-sync above: the container ignore rules
# do not exclude .local/bin, so containers received this wrapper too.
.local/bin/claude-glm

# The ydotool capability was removed, so dot_config/systemd/user/ydotool.service
# and dot_local/libexec/executable_ydotoold-active-seat no longer have sources.
# Deleting those sources stopped chezmoi managing them but left the
# already-deployed unit and wrapper behind — prune them here.
#
# ORDER MATTERS on a live host, and docs/decommission/ydotool.md leads with it:
# the wrapper below is the unit's ExecStart target, so pruning it while the unit
# is still enabled and running risks a Restart=on-failure re-exec into a missing
# path and a start-limit-hit failure. Stop and disable the unit BEFORE the first
# apply. That checklist also owns everything else chezmoi must never do — unmask
# the root service, remove the package.
#
# GATED to the hosts that actually received the targets, mirroring the
# .chezmoiignore predicate that deployed them (Fedora Linux, KDE or GNOME, not
# headless, not a container). An ungated prune would delete a same-named unit or
# wrapper that a headless, non-Fedora, or container host owns and chezmoi never
# put there — a real risk here, because ~/.config/systemd/user/ydotool.service is
# the path third-party ydotool guides tell users to hand-author.
#
# The gate is deliberately kept this tight even though it costs completeness:
# `headless` is a hook fact whose absentDefault is true, so a first apply, or a
# host that went headless after deployment, silently prunes nothing and chezmoi
# still exits 0. Loosening the predicate would widen a provenance-blind delete
# onto hosts that never received the files, which is the worse trade. The
# checklist closes the gap instead: it has the operator confirm both paths are
# gone after the apply and remove them by hand if not.
{{- if and (eq .chezmoi.os "linux") (eq $f.distro "fedora") (or (eq $f.desktop "kde") (eq $f.desktop "gnome")) (not $f.headless) (not $f.container) }}
.config/systemd/user/ydotool.service
.local/libexec/ydotoold-active-seat
{{- end }}

# The docker-credential-gh / docker-credential-glab helpers were retired:
# ~/.config/containers/auth.json now carries stored base64("user:PAT") keys
# rendered from 1Password (dot_config/containers/private_auth.json.tmpl)
# instead of delegating to `gh` / `glab auth docker-helper` per pull. Deleting
# the sources stopped managing them but left the already-deployed executables
# behind — prune them here. There is NO container gate: the container ignore
# rules do not exclude .local/bin, so containers received these binaries too
# and must prune them.
.local/bin/docker-credential-gh
.local/bin/docker-credential-glab

# The unmanaged-repo-guard omp plugin was removed, so
# dot_local/share/omp-plugins/plugins/unmanaged-repo-guard/ no longer has a
# source. Deleting that source stopped chezmoi managing the tree but left the
# already-deployed copy behind — prune it here. A directory entry removes the
# tree recursively and leaves the .omp-plugin/marketplace.json catalog root
# untouched.
#
# There is NO container gate: the container skip never covered the guard tree,
# so containers received it too and must prune it. Every managed OS received it
# as well, so no host class is exempt and a gate would only create one that
# never converges. A host that never
# applied between the guard's introduction and its removal simply takes this
# as a no-op.
#
# The omp-installed copy under ~/.omp/plugins was never chezmoi-managed and is
# the operator's to remove. The plugin's runtime state was never deployed either
# — prune it like the runtime-created .agents/skills/ce-* entries above.
.local/share/omp-plugins/plugins/unmanaged-repo-guard
.local/state/unmanaged-repo-guard

# The local h82-dotfiles marketplace was omp's alone and its source is gone, so
# the catalog chezmoi deployed is un-written here on every host rather than only
# in containers. Anything else under ~/.local/share/omp-plugins/ was installed by
# omp, not by chezmoi, and belongs to the operator checklist.
.local/share/omp-plugins/.omp-plugin/marketplace.json

# Solaar was retired, so dot_config/solaar/rules.yaml.tmpl
# no longer has a source. Deleting that source stopped chezmoi managing it but
# leaves the already-deployed ~/.config/solaar/rules.yaml copy behind — prune it here.
.config/solaar/rules.yaml

# Claude Desktop autostart was decommissioned; deleting the source stops managing it
# but leaves the already-deployed copy behind — prune it here.
.config/autostart/claude-desktop.desktop
